    "['arp [ip_address] [mac_address] [encapsulation_type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system arp static 10.1.2.2 l2-interface ge-1/0/1 mac 00:e0:fc:41:03:02', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Cisco ARP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system arp static 10.1.2.2 l2-interface ge-1/0/1 mac 00:e0:fc:41:03:02\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses a different syntax where ARP entries are configured under the system hierarchy\\n- The MAC address format changes from Cisco\\'s \"00e0.fc41.0302\" to Juniper\\'s \"00:e0:fc:41:03:02\"\\n- The interface name changes from \"GigabitEthernet1/0/1\" to Juniper\\'s \"ge-1/0/1\" format\\n- The \"ARPA\" encapsulation type is implied as default in Juniper and doesn\\'t need explicit configuration', 'trans_template': 'set system arp static 10.1.2.2 l2-interface ge-1/0/1 mac 00:e0:fc:41:03:02'}]]": 1,
    "['arp [ip_address] [mac_address] [encapsulation_type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.3 arp 00:e0:fc:41:03:04', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.3 arp 00:e0:fc:41:03:04\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, ARP entries are configured under the interface\\'s address family configuration\\n2. The format is: `set interfaces <interface-name> unit 0 family inet address <ip-address> arp <mac-address>`\\n3. The MAC address format is converted to Juniper\\'s standard colon-separated format\\n4. The interface naming follows Juniper\\'s convention (ge-1/0/2 instead of GigabitEthernet1/0/2)\\n5. The \"ARPA\" encapsulation type is implied in Juniper\\'s Ethernet interfaces and doesn\\'t need explicit configuration', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.3 arp 00:e0:fc:41:03:04'}]]": 1,
